  "content": "Insurance claims totaling Rs 23.22 billion registered so far; payments reach Rs 1.58 billion\nRastriya Samachar Samiti (RSS)\nSunday, October 12, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 12\nFollowing the Gen-Z protests on September 8 and 9, the physical structures that sustained damage have filed insurance claims amounting to Rs 23 billion 227 million 800 thousand. As per the latest information from the Nepal Insurance Authority, non-life insurance companies have disbursed payments totaling Rs 1 billion 585 million 600 thousand.\nReports indicate that these payments were expedited due to the proactive measures taken by the Authority to ensure that insurance funds were made available swiftly.\nTo date, the Authority has recorded a total of 3,099 insurance claim applications. Among the claims, 153 are property insurance claims, 2,206 are motor insurance claims, 190 are engineering and contract risk insurance claims, 12 are transport insurance claims, and 38 are other insurance claims.\nIn Koshi Province, 396 claims have been submitted, in Madhesh 355, in Bagmati 1,669, in Gandaki 212, in Lumbini 246, in Karnali 22, and in Sudurpashchim Province 199. This data is current as of October 9. The Authority reports that Siddhartha Insurance Company has received the highest claims, totaling Rs 5 billion 614 million 400 thousand. The company has disbursed Rs 594.4 million to the policyholders.\\\nAdditionally, The Oriental Insurance has received claims amounting to Rs 5 billion 244 million 700 thousand, with payments of Rs 570 thousand made. IGE Prudential Insurance has claims worth Rs 2 billion 759 million 700 thousand, and has distributed Rs 304.3 million to the insured. Shikhar Insurance has reported an insurance claim of Rs 2 billion 408 million 600 thousand, with Rs 319.4 million already made available.\nCurrently, there are 18 non-life insurance companies, including micro insurance firms, operating nationwide.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\ngold\nnepali cricket\nflood\nSushila Karki\ninsurance\nministers\nICC T20 World Cup Qualifier\nRastriya Samachar Samiti (RSS)\nRSS is a government-run national news portal of Nepal.\nMore From the Author\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nHealth insurance amount to be raised to Rs 500,000\n9 months ago\nOnly 41% of Nepalis are insured: Insurance Board\n3 years ago\nThird party insurance amount for families of road accident victims to double\n7 years ago\nExperts criticise new Insurance Bill\n7 years ago\nMost Read\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\n12 stranded backpackers rescued from Langtang\nWhen a joke fuels division: Casual hate speech and the Gen Z revolution in Nepal\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n4 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n4 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nSociety\nFear among Raute community after drunk intruders enter settlement; security demanded\n3 hours ago\nCricket\nNepal to face UAE in Super Six clash of ICC T20 World Cup Qualifier\n3 hours ago\nOpinion\nThe rise of Nepal’s first woman Prime Minister\n7 hours ago\nPolitics\nWho do student unions stand for? Questions rise after Gen Z 